  "question": {
    "text": "System shown in figure is in equilibrium and at rest. The spring and string are massless, now the string is cut. The acceleration of mass $2 m$ and $m$ just after the string is cut will be\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/F_gWz2vcxbWlp6GGjRBL5jHFqffW0hYXVd6i_8l9-YM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5dELI",
      "text": "\n$g / 2$ upwards, $g$ downwards\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "nD0md",
      "text": "\n$g$ upwards, $g / 2$ downwards\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oiXJR",
      "text": "\n$g$ upwards, $2 g$ downwards\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8DvWf",
      "text": "\n$2 g$ upwards, $g$ downwards",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Initially under equilibrium of mass ' $m$ '\n$$\nT=m g\n$$\nNow, the string is cut. Therefore, $T=m g$ force is decreased on mass $m$ upwards and downwards on mass $2 m$.\n$$\na_m=\\frac{m g}{m}=g \\text { (downwards) and }\n$$\n$$\na_{2 m}=\\frac{m g}{2 m}=\\frac{g}{2} \\text { (upwards) }\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
